---
# Web UI, reached only through the IngressRoute (Authelia-gated) — the macro targets a
# Service named after the containers_list entry.
#
# Pinned to instance 1 ONLY (`instance: pihole`), unlike pihole-dns below. Pi-hole v6 keeps
# admin sessions in FTL's own memory, so a session round-robined across two independent FTLs
# 401s at random, and homepage's widget polling would report whichever pod it happened to
# hit — half the real query volume, flapping between refreshes. The admin UI is a
# single-user surface, so pinning it costs nothing. DNS stays load-balanced across both
# instances because each query is stateless and redundancy is the point. Don't "fix" this
# inconsistency without re-reading why the split exists.
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: pihole
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
spec:
  selector:
    app: pihole
    instance: pihole
  ports:
    - name: web
      port: {{ container_item.port }}
      targetPort: {{ container_item.port }}
---
# Instance 2's web port, and the ONLY caller is pihole-exporter. Added 2026-09-10 for issue
# #1444: DNS is load-balanced across two independent FTLs, each keeping its own pihole-FTL.db,
# so a metrics scrape that reached only the Service above would report roughly HALF the house's
# query volume — silently, and with a plausible-looking graph. There is no IngressRoute for it
# and there must not be one: the reason the admin UI is pinned to instance 1 (see above) is that
# a session round-robined across two FTLs 401s at random, and a second route would reintroduce
# exactly that.
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: pihole-2-web
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
spec:
  selector:
    app: pihole
    instance: pihole-2
  ports:
    - name: web
      port: {{ container_item.port }}
      targetPort: {{ container_item.port }}
---
# The LAN DNS seam (slice-6 D4): one pinned VIP the router's DHCP DNS option flips to at
# cutover. Both Pi-holes serve simultaneously while leases renew — the free strangler.
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: pihole-dns
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
  annotations:
    metallb.io/loadBalancerIPs: {{ pihole_k8s_lan_ip }}
spec:
  type: LoadBalancer
  # Pinned because CoreDNS forwards here by address — see k3s_coredns_upstreams.
  clusterIP: {{ pihole_k8s_dns_cluster_ip }}
  # Preserves real client addresses — Pi-hole's per-client query log is how the drain is
  # observed (retire the Docker copy only when ITS log flatlines, and this one shows who
  # has moved). Safe on a single node.
  externalTrafficPolicy: Local
  selector:
    app: pihole
  ports:
    - name: dns-udp
      port: 53
      targetPort: 53
      protocol: UDP
    - name: dns-tcp
      port: 53
      targetPort: 53
      protocol: TCP
